---
title: "failed_remediation_protocol (Legion: Incident Response Plan)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_detect: remediation_failed OR new_bug_introduced
    q_detect --> q_pause_frontend: pause existing frontend
    q_pause_frontend --> q_block_interaction: users cannot interact with protocol
    q_block_interaction --> q_emergency_withdraw: perform emergencyWithdraw on all active sale contracts
    q_emergency_withdraw --> q_secure_funds: funds secured from active contracts
    q_secure_funds --> q_implement_fix: implement required changes
    q_implement_fix --> q_audit: deploy to partner auditing company for audit
    q_audit --> q_deploy: audit passed
    q_audit --> q_implement_fix: audit found issues
    q_deploy --> q_resume_frontend: deploy new contract instance
    q_resume_frontend --> [*]: frontend resumed, protocol accessible

    note right of q_pause_frontend
        INV-001: Frontend MUST be paused before any fund operations
        INV-002: No user interaction with protocol while frontend is paused
    end note

    note right of q_emergency_withdraw
        INV-003: emergencyWithdraw MUST cover ALL active sale contracts
        INV-004: Funds must be secured before any code changes are implemented
    end note

    note right of q_deploy
        INV-005: New contracts MUST be audited before deployment
        INV-006: Deployment is automated through AWS
    end note
